<title>INDIA: India approves Westinghouse investment.</title>
<headline>India approves Westinghouse investment.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian government said on Monday it had approved a proposal by U.S.-based Westinghouse Electric Corp to take a $12.5-million stake in a power project in the northern state of Uttar Pradesh.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the Cabinet Committee on Foreign Investment approved a foreign investment of 898.8 million rupees ($25 million) split evenly between Westinghouse and Econo Power International Corp of the Cayman Islands.</p>
<p>The committee approved the proposal on Sunday.</p>
<p>The foreign investment would represent a 31 percent stake in the project's total equity of 2.9 billion rupees, it said.</p>
<p>The power project is being set up in Aligarh by Wasan Electric Power Generation Ltd, it said.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
